        "original_id": "a4142ebb-9703-5cdc-ad86-01aa90ec8ceb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Johnny Herbert, Rubens Barrichello\n- Organizations: Stewart Grand Prix, WilliamsF1\n- Products: Williams FW31, Lotus-Ford\n- Events: 1992 Formula One Indoor Trophy, 1995 Formula One championship, 1999 Formula One season, European Grand Prix, French Grand Prix, Constructors' Championship\n- Topics: Formula One\n\nFacts:\n- Johnny Herbert was born on 25 June 1964 and is a British racing driver.\n- Johnny Herbert won the 1992 Formula One Indoor Trophy in a Lotus-Ford.\n- Johnny Herbert placed fourth in the 1995 Formula One championship.\n- Stewart Grand Prix had its strongest season in 1999, with Johnny Herbert winning the European Grand Prix and Rubens Barrichello taking pole position at the French Grand Prix.\n- Stewart Grand Prix finished fourth overall in the 1999 Constructors' Championship.\n- Johnny Herbert raced in Formula One from 1989 to 2000 for seven different teams and won three races.\n- The Williams FW31 is a Formula One motor racing car designed and built by WilliamsF1.",
